  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="red" data-hint="Find the color adjective that appears after the noun car." data-fix="a red car" data-why="The adjective goes before the noun, so red comes before car: a red car, not a car red.">
    <h3>Drill 7: fix the word order</h3>
    <p>Tap the adjective that must move before the noun.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="a">a</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="car">car</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="red">red</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="greens" data-hint="Two makes the noun doors plural; check whether the color adjective should also change." data-fix="two green doors" data-why="A descriptive adjective does not take plural -s. The noun is plural (doors), but the adjective stays green, not greens.">
    <h3>Drill 8: fix the adjective</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="two">two</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="greens">greens</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="doors">doors</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 9: fix the order, then say it</h3>
    <p>Say the correct phrase or sentence aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> a bag blue &nbsp;→&nbsp; put the color in order</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>a blue bag</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> a watch expensive &nbsp;→&nbsp; put it in order</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>an expensive watch</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> The is car new. &nbsp;→&nbsp; fix the sentence</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The car is new.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> two whites shirts &nbsp;→&nbsp; remove the wrong -s</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>two white shirts</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> a notebook small black &nbsp;→&nbsp; size + color + noun</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>a small black notebook</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A new office</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“My new office is nice. The walls are white and the door is brown. I have a big black desk and two green chairs. My favorite thing is the small red lamp.”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You identified the white walls, two green chairs, and small red lamp from the office description.">
    <h3>Read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="white" data-hint="The second sentence describes both the walls and the door." data-fix="The walls are white.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. What color are the walls?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="white">white</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="brown">brown</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="black">black</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="two" data-hint="The third sentence gives the number immediately before green chairs." data-fix="The office has two green chairs.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. How many green chairs are there?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two">two</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="one">one</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three">three</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the lamp" data-hint="The final noun phrase is the small red lamp." data-fix="The lamp is red.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. What is red?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the lamp">the lamp</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the desk">the desk</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the door">the door</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="note"><strong>Choice and privacy:</strong> you do not need to describe your possessions, clothes, home, or appearance. Use a classroom object, a picture, or invented information whenever you prefer.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A phone in a picture:</b> Describe it with one color and one quality. <span class="ex">The phone is black and new. It is a new black phone.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A vehicle:</b> Choose a real or invented car, bike, bus, or train. Compare it with another vehicle. <span class="ex">The bus is big and slow. The bike is small and fast.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Clothes in a picture:</b> Name three items and add a second identifier to one. <span class="ex">I can see a blue shirt, black shoes, and the brown jacket on the left.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A room:</b> Describe a real, pictured, or invented room. <span class="ex">The office is big. The chairs are gray. The old desk is near the door.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A city:</b> Compare two features with an explicit reference point. <span class="ex">The downtown buses are slow at 5 p.m. The north park is big compared with the other parks.</span></div>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: identify the lost item</h3>
    <p>Use three fictional lost-and-found items: <span class="ex">a small black notebook labeled “A,” a big blue bag by the window, and two old gray keys on the desk.</span> Describe one item without naming it. Your partner identifies it and reads the full description back. Then switch.</p>
    <p><strong>Success criteria:</strong> use both adjective positions; keep adjectives unchanged with plural nouns; use size or age before color; connect two qualities after <em>be</em> with <span class="ex">and</span>; and include a label or location so color is not the only clue.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the choice</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “For the words in this lesson, an adjective can go ______ the noun, like <strong>a ____ car</strong>. It can also come after ______, like <strong>The car is ____</strong>. A descriptive adjective does not change for a ______ noun, so I say <strong>two red cars</strong>.”</p>
    <p>Then say one real or invented sentence about something <strong>near</strong> you using a color, and one using a quality word like <em>big</em>, <em>new</em>, or <em>good</em>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great. You can place an adjective before a noun and after be, and you know the colors and common opposites.">
    <h3>Final quiz: colors, opposites, and word order</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a red car" data-hint="Before a noun, place the color adjective between the article and noun." data-fix="a red car">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Which phrase has the article, color adjective, and noun in standard order?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a red car">a red car</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a car red">a car red</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a reds car">a reds car</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="old" data-hint="Choose the age word that contrasts with new." data-fix="new ↔ old">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What is the opposite of <em>new</em>?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="old">old</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="small">small</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="cold">cold</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="two green doors" data-hint="Two makes door plural, while the adjective green stays unchanged." data-fix="two green doors">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Which is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two green doors">two green doors</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two greens doors">two greens doors</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two door greens">two door greens</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="expensive" data-hint="Compare the $900 price with the buyer's $100 budget." data-fix="For this buyer, the watch is expensive.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. My watch budget is $100, but this watch costs $900. For me, it is ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="cheap">cheap</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="expensive">expensive</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="short">short</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The coffee is hot." data-hint="A complete description places is between the subject and adjective." data-fix="The coffee is hot.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. The coffee just came out of the machine. Which complete sentence places the adjective after <em>be</em>?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The coffee is hot.">The coffee is hot.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The coffee hot.">The coffee hot.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The coffee hot is.">The coffee hot is.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a small black notebook" data-hint="For this lesson's pattern, size comes before color, and both come before the noun." data-fix="a small black notebook">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. Which order is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a small black notebook">a small black notebook</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a black small notebook">a black small notebook</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a notebook small black">a notebook small black</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The notebook is small and black." data-hint="The subject is one notebook with both qualities, so use is and connect the adjectives with and." data-fix="The notebook is small and black.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. One notebook has both qualities: small and black. Which sentence reports exactly that?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The notebook is small and black.">The notebook is small and black.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The notebook is small or black.">The notebook is small or black.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The notebooks are small and black.">The notebooks are small and black.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="slow" data-hint="For the same route, sixty minutes is longer than twenty minutes." data-fix="Compared with the express bus, the local bus is slow.">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. For the same route, the express bus takes 20 minutes and the local bus takes 60. The local bus is ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="fast">fast</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="slow">slow</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="big">big</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check quiz</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset quiz</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

